.................
.................
STEP 0 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files -- Creating directory & copying some files.
.................
.................
mkdir 4.<next_number>_work_in_progress
cp -r 4.<current_number>_work_in_progress/creation_scripts  4.<next_number>_work_in_progress
cp -r 4.<current_number>/verilog  4.<next_number>_work_in_progress/verilog

Edit 4.<next_number>_work_in_progress/verilog/verilog.v
to create any new modules.

cd 4.<next_number>_work_in_progress/creation_scripts  for all subsequent steps until the NEXT_TO_LAST_STEP

.................
.................
STEP 1 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files
.................
.................
run_libcomp

This creates a local libcomp.atpglib file from the ../verilog/adk.v  file, 
   as well as important output files to examine.
Examine the screen output or end of file verify.results to ensure all models have 100% coverage, no mismatches.
Currently, that looks like the lines between double quotes below:
"
***** Fault (pessimistic) Coverage Summary by Decile ***** 
 See file fault_coverage_0_to_10_percent_models for a list
 of models in 0 to 10% decile, etc. for each nonNULL decile.
   100%      --  143 models.
---------------------------------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------
Verification Summary:
   143 Total Models
ALL PASSED for all patterns.
"

.................
.................
STEP 2 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files
.................
.................
Before making this run, add any tessent attributes (if needed) for new cells to cell.map in this directory.
Send mail to don_ross@mentor.com  if you are in doubt.

run_fs_tessent
diff fs_tessent_last_release.log  fs_tessent.log

.................
.................
OPTIONAL STEP 3 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files.  Verify pad.lib, scang.lib, cell.lib
.................
.................
Some LV applications consume pad.lib, scang.lib, cell.lib created from tessent cell library just built.
However, more and more are using TCL or library API, so this is becoming an optional step.

CAVEAT: JF's active Low enable clock gaters (cgand0 & cgor0) are not supported by scang.
Therefore, run_all is no longer valid, and has been moved to run_all.obsolete

cgand0 and cgor0 must be commented out of the adk.tcelllib for etlibgen to succeed.

Step3 A.
Manually comment out model cgand0 as well as model cgor0 in local adk.tcelllib using /* */
Note that ../adk.tcelllib can be moved to tessent/adk.tcelllib if all steps OK.

Step3 B.
run_etlibcertify

At the bottom of etlibcertify.log, that file will name two outDir/ logs that should be examined or diffed against :
scanCellSummary_last_release.final
padCellSummary_last_release.final

If OK. (no or expected changes)
 mv the new .final files to local files of above name (clean destroys them otherwise).

.................
.................
STEP 4 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files.  Verifying the Liberty.
.................
.................
First, make corresponding changes to the liberty/adk.lib file.  There is no automation to do this.

Second, verify that DC accepts it using (in the same directory as the new ADK Liberty file):
run_dc_shell

See run_dc_shell for comments on how to check that everything is OK.

CAVEAT: This reuses fastscan.do.cat and overwrites sim.log from run_libcomp, so make sure
        you are done with run_libcomp results, and have examined sim.log before doing this step.
        run_libcomp is the first step of run_all.

Third, verify Liberty against the Verilog by :
A. run/source verify_liberty_step_1  to create only_liberty.atpglib
B. edit fastscan.do.cat from earlier run_libcomp run and change :
   write netlist design.v -verilog -rep -positional   to :
   write netlist design.v -verilog -rep
C. run/source verify_liberty_step_2  to verify Liberty against Verilog
   Check bottom of sim.log to ensure no simulation mismatches.
   Note that any Liberty with statetables (clock gaters and synchronizer_cells) will have 0% coverage,
     and that verification is meaningless for those, because ATPG produced only X (dont compare) for them.

Fourth, if everything OK :
mv adk.lib ../liberty/adk.lib  in new directory.

Hopefully, there will be another README created by Jack Zhamkochyan and others on how to create the other files.
mv adk.db ../synopsys.adk.db
  only if those other README files do not exist.  We have never used the .db from my run_dc_shell so far.

.................
.................
STEP 5 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files.  To help person doing next release.
.................
.................
run clean in this directory to cleanup the intermediate files created.
mv fs_tessent.log fs_tessent_last_release.log  // So next person has something to compare to.


.................
.................
STEP 6 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files.  Edit & move adk.tcelllib to final location.
.................
.................
cd ..   
   (so now just above creation_scripts/ directory) -- there you will see adk.tcelllib

Edit adk.tcelllib and very near the top, change "dft_cell_selection ( default )" to "dft_cell_selection ( adk_typ )".
  Note that this adk.tcelllib was created equal to one in creation_scripts/ but was not edited to do etlibcertify run, so safer to use it.

Then move that file adk.tcelllib to tessent/adk.tcelllib in new directory :
mv adk.tcelllib tessent/adk.tcelllib


.................
.................
STEP 7 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files.
.................
.................
cp -r 4.<current_number>/synthesis_helpers 4.<new_number>_work_in_progress


If it does not already exist :
mkdir 4.<new_number>_work_in_progress/synopsys

cp 4.<current_number>/synopsys/*.setup 4.<new_number>_work_in_progress/synopsys
Edit the 2 .setup files and change 4.<current_number> to 4.<new_number> in those 2 files.


Notify Jack Zhamkochyan that another rev is needed, or follow the other README files to complete the release.
